{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3316","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3316","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3316\",\"parent_revision\":\"6ce8a4e419f128aaa7dda9d27a31f6d9d6916d5fa4de4982393fb1616ca80521\",\"root_revision\":\"6ce8a4e419f128aaa7dda9d27a31f6d9d6916d5fa4de4982393fb1616ca80521\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nplugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md, System Error procedure step 3, builds a new backlog item's description as:\\n\\n\\\"System error encountered during grooming of <item_ref/>:\\\\nTool {tool name} returned: {error text}.\\\\nContext: {stage}, {what was being attempted}.\\\"\\n\\n{error text} is the exact, unsanitized text of an MCP tool's error response, interpolated with no quoting/fencing/escaping. MCP tool responses can originate from less-trusted backends (e.g. a third-party issue tracker integration) or reflect attacker-influenced input (e.g. a crafted issue title/body that triggers a particular error path), so this creates a path for crafted instruction-like text to flow, unsanitized, into a newly created backlog item's description \u2014 which is itself later read by other AI agents (groomers, planners, task-workers) as trusted-ish input.\\n\\nThis is a pre-existing pattern, not introduced by #3276's changes \u2014 groom/error.md's diff for #3276 only touched the separate \\\"Agent Failure\\\" procedure (its own steps 3-5), not this \\\"System Error\\\" procedure. Same underlying risk class as the prompt-injection finding already fixed in #3276/PR #3286 for implement-feature/SKILL.md's contract-verification dispatch (unfenced interpolation of untrusted-provenance content into an instruction context read by an AI agent).\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Flagged by qg-T0 (dh:multi-perspective-review, security perspective) during #3276's Quality Gate T0, as a non-blocking MINOR finding outside that PR's diff scope\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a0b691b118cbc969681752e079e9a01949f9d3b689038d75783b53c3b1a085f7\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRZ5KOw\"}"}